# A road runs on past a street's last plot. A new street never runs over
# another road's end without a crossroads: it ends short of it instead.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> build crossroads at s0:28
  #1 intersection at s0:28-30, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:29 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> ride +27
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #61 intersection at s1:157-159, done
> ride #last
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s2:131 facing +
> ride +27
  rider: s2:158 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #97 intersection at s2:157-159, done
# the third street runs south at column 2, past the main street's west end
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 10..252
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #61
  s3  runs south (lots on its east side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #97
    crossroads #1: s0:29 = s1:131 (cell A29)
    crossroads #61: s1:158 = s2:131 (cell AB29)
    crossroads #97: s2:158 = s3:131 (cell AB2)
